<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">SWAPO</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1960">1960</a>–</span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a> · Also known as South West Africa People's Organisation</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">SWAPO, the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/namibia">South West Africa</a> People's Organisation, is the Namibian liberation movement founded in 1960. From 1966 its armed wing fought South African rule in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/south-african-border-war">South African Border War</a>, operating from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/zambia">Zambia</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/angola">Angola</a>. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-nations">United Nations</a> recognised it as the representative of the Namibian people, and it has governed Namibia since independence in 1990.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/swapo.jpg" alt="SWAPO" width="320" height="213" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Original by Bries · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_South_West_Africa_People%27s_Organisation.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote>From 1966 the army fought the <b>South West African People’s Organisation</b> in the South African Border War, which spread into Angola after 1975, when South African forces intervened in the Angolan civil war against the MPLA government and its Cuban allies.</blockquote><a href="/empire/republic-of-south-africa">Republic of South Africa · Military</a></li><li><blockquote><b>SWAPO</b> waged an armed struggle from 1966, linked to the war in Angola.</blockquote><a href="/state/south-west-africa">South West Africa</a></li></ul></section>
